//TC-O(n)
//SC-O(1)
class Solution {
    public int lengthOfLongestSubstring(String s) {
        int maxLength = 0;
        HashMap<Character, Integer> map = new HashMap<>();
        int start = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {
            char ch = s.charAt(i);
            if (map.containsKey(ch)) {
                start = Math.max(start, map.get(ch) + 1);
            }
            maxLength = Math.max(maxLength, i - start + 1);
            map.put(ch, i);
        }
        return maxLength;
    }
}
/**
Approach
There are two pointers. Start and i (end)
We are trying to form a window and calculate the length of that window.
Start will be at the first index, and I moves on every character. If that character is not present in the map, the calculate the maximum length between eye and start.
If the character is present in the Hashmap, then the start has to be moved to skip that duplicate. The start will be moved by the previous seen index +1. To avoid moving backwards, start should be moved between math.Maks of start and the previous scene index +1.

